    {
      "alt": "Sete Cidades Lagoon on São Miguel in the Azores",
      "credit": "Gonçalo Torres · CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "São Miguel is a volcanic Atlantic island of crater lakes, green ridges and geothermal pools, making it a strong match for hiking, water and wellness. Late spring through early autumn offers longer daylight for viewpoints and trails, though fast-changing island weather still rewards a flexible plan. A week gives enough room for active days and a weather buffer. Expect a mid-range budget, with transport and guided activities often costing more than walks and viewpoints. Hike near Sete Cidades, follow a coastal route, visit a tea-growing landscape, soak in a thermal pool and keep one quiet day for a village or rain-day museum.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/azores-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "name": "São Miguel",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_overlooking_the_Sete_Cidades_Lagoon,_S%C3%A3o_Miguel_island,_Azores_(Portugal).jpg",
