        }
      ],
      "words": 102
    },
    {
      "alt": "Tegalalang rice terraces near Ubud in Bali",
      "credit": "chensiyuan · CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Ubud is an inland Balinese town surrounded by villages, rice landscapes and craft traditions, making it a useful base for food, wellness and gentle nature time. Summer into early autumn is typically the drier period for walks and day trips, although popular areas stay busy. A week works well; ten days lets travellers slow down and avoid daily long drives. It is a lower-budget idea for meals and local services, with private transport and polished retreats adding cost. Walk a rice-field path, visit a temple or craft village respectfully, take a cooking class, browse a market and balance outings with a massage, garden café or quiet pool afternoon.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/bali-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "name": "Ubud",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_Tegalalang_rice_terrace_ubud_bali.jpg",
          "label": "chensiyuan"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
          "label": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 108
    },
    {
      "alt": "Hungarian Parliament beside the Danube in Budapest",
      "credit": "Pierre Blaché · CC0",
      "description": "Budapest spans both sides of the Danube, combining grand architecture, layered history, museums and thermal-bath culture in an easy city-break format. Spring and autumn favour long walks, while winter makes indoor collections, cafés and baths especially appealing. Three or four days covers the essentials; five to seven days supports a slower pace and more neighbourhood time. It is the collection’s lower-budget European city idea, though river-view lodging and major attractions raise costs. Walk the Buda hills and Pest boulevards, tour a historic building, visit a museum, spend a few hours at a bath and finish with an evening along the river.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/budapest-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC0",
      "name": "Budapest",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hungarian_Parliament_Building_2023-9.jpg",
          "label": "Pierre Blaché"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
          "label": "CC0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 101
    },
    {
      "alt": "Ornate Buddhist temple in Chiang Mai",
      "credit": "Philip Nalangan · CC BY 4.0",
      "description": "Chiang Mai is a northern Thai city where temple architecture, markets, craft communities and a renowned food culture support both cultural discovery and a relaxed wellness break. The cooler, drier winter season is the easiest time for walking and outdoor day trips; travellers should still check current air-quality and local conditions before booking. Stay five to seven days, or longer for a slower regional base. It is a lower-budget idea for food and local transport, with workshops and retreats adding cost. Visit old-city temples respectfully, browse an evening market, take a cooking class, explore a craft district and set aside a restorative spa or café afternoon.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/chiang-mai-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "name": "Chiang Mai",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chiang_Mai_Temple_Thailand.jpg",
          "label": "Philip Nalangan"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
          "label": "CC BY 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 106
    },
    {
      "alt": "A footpath through Monteverde cloud forest in Costa Rica",
      "credit": "Cephas · CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Monteverde is a highland cloud-forest area where misty trails, dense biodiversity and conservation-focused reserves make wildlife and hiking the centre of the trip. The drier stretch from winter into spring generally makes trails and views easier to plan, while forest weather can remain changeable. Give the area three or four nights inside a seven-to-ten-day Costa Rica itinerary. It is a higher-budget nature stop once transfers, reserve tickets and guided walks are included. Join an early wildlife walk, hike a reserve trail, cross a canopy bridge, visit a conservation or coffee project and leave time for a quiet evening as the forest changes after dark.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/costa-rica-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "name": "Monteverde",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monteverde_Reserve_Costa_Rica_02.jpg",
          "label": "Cephas"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
          "label": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 104
    },
    {
      "alt": "Rocky coast at Agioi Apostoloi in Crete",
      "credit": "Ввласенко · CC BY-SA 3.0",
      "description": "Crete is a large Mediterranean island where beaches, mountain villages, archaeological landscapes and a produce-led food tradition support both relaxed and cultural trips. Late spring and early autumn are especially comfortable for combining the coast with walking; summer best suits travellers prioritising warm-water beach days. Spend at least a week in one region, or ten to fourteen days for a broader route. The budget is mid-range, with car hire and inter-town travel shaping costs. Swim in a sheltered bay, visit an archaeological site, eat in a village taverna, walk a gorge or coastal trail and browse a harbour town in the evening.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/crete-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
      "name": "Crete",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coast_in_Agioi_apostoli._Crete,_Greece.jpg",
          "label": "Ввласенко"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/",
          "label": "CC BY-SA 3.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 102
    },
    {
      "alt": "Edinburgh skyline and castle ridge",
      "credit": "Andrew Colin · CC BY 2.0",
      "description": "Edinburgh is a compact hill city of stone closes, major museums, literary history and dramatic viewpoints, blending culture and architecture with accessible nature. Late spring through early autumn brings longer daylight for walking; summer is lively but often busier, while shoulder seasons feel calmer. Plan three or four days, or a week with a coastal or countryside outing. It is a higher-budget city break, particularly for central lodging and festival-period stays. Walk the Old and New Towns, tour the castle area, choose a national collection, climb a suitable hill or viewpoint and leave time for a bookshop, café and neighbourhood pub.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/edinburgh-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "name": "Edinburgh",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Edinburgh.jpg",
          "label": "Andrew Colin"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/",
          "label": "CC BY 2.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 101
    },
    {
      "alt": "Dry-sand garden at Ginkaku-ji temple in Kyoto",
      "credit": "Basile Morin · CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Kyoto is a former imperial capital shaped by temples, gardens, traditional craft and distinctive regional food, which fits culture, cuisine and a contemplative pace. Spring brings blossoms and autumn brings vivid foliage, so either season rewards time outdoors while also attracting more visitors. Plan five to seven days, or extend the stay to explore at a gentler rhythm. It is a higher-budget idea once central lodging, rail travel and admissions are included. Visit one temple district early, walk a garden, browse Nishiki-area food stalls, see a craft or museum collection and reserve an unhurried evening for a neighbourhood meal.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/kyoto-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "name": "Kyoto",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dry-sand_Zen_garden_made_of_beige_stripes_a_sunny_day_at_Higashiyama_Jisho-ji_Buddhist_temple_Ginkaku-ji_Kyoto_Japan.jpg",
          "label": "Basile Morin"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
          "label": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 99
    },
    {
      "alt": "Lisbon skyline from Miradouro de São Pedro de Alcântara at twilight",
      "credit": "Dale Cruse · CC BY 4.0",
      "description": "Lisbon is a hilly riverside capital where tiled façades, historic quarters and a strong café culture make architecture, walking and food natural themes. Spring and autumn usually suit long days outside without relying on peak-summer heat. Allow three or four days for a city break, or a week with slower neighbourhood days and a nearby excursion. The budget is mid-range: simple bakeries and public transport balance paid sights and central stays. Walk Alfama and Baixa, ride to a viewpoint, browse a market, visit a museum and leave an evening for petiscos by the Tagus.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/lisbon-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "name": "Lisbon",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
          "href": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lisbon_Skyline_from_Miradouro_de_S%C3%A3o_Pedro_de_Alc%C3%A2ntara_at_Twilight_(54714276547).jpg",
          "label": "Dale Cruse"
        },
        {
          "href": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
          "label": "CC BY 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "words": 94
    },
    {
      "alt": "Petit-Champlain district in Québec City at night",
      "credit": "Wilfredor · CC0",
      "description": "Québec City is a compact fortified city with steep old streets, French-speaking culture and a regional food scene, so walking, architecture and cuisine fit naturally together. Summer offers long outdoor days, autumn brings colour, and winter turns the historic centre into a cold-weather city break that needs warm indoor pauses. Allow three to four days, or a week with surrounding countryside. This is a higher-budget idea because central stays, dining and regional transport add up. Walk the upper and lower town, explore Petit-Champlain, visit a history collection, try local dishes and reserve time for a riverside viewpoint or nearby nature outing.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/quebec-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC0",
      "name": "Québec City",
      "sourceLinks": [
        {
