    {
      "alt": "Aerial view of Lake Bohinj and the Julian Alps",
      "credit": "Carsten Steger · CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Lake Bohinj is an alpine base inside a broad mountain landscape, well suited to nature, hiking, water activities and genuinely quiet downtime. Late spring through early autumn gives the widest choice of lakeside walks and higher routes; conditions can change quickly, so plans should match experience and forecasts. A long weekend covers the lake, while five to seven days allows rest and weather flexibility. It is a mid-range stay, with accommodation and lifts or guided outings the main extras. Circle part of the shore, take a gentle valley walk, paddle or swim where permitted, visit a waterfall and keep an afternoon simply for the lake.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/slovenia-hero.webp",
      "imageLoaded": true,
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "name": "Lake Bohinj",
      "sourceLinks": [
