    {
      "alt": "City of Arts and Sciences in Valencia",
      "credit": "Arthurguo · CC BY-SA 3.0",
      "description": "Valencia pairs a historic Mediterranean city with contemporary architecture, gardens, markets and an urban beach, so city-break, food and water themes can share one itinerary. Spring and autumn are comfortable for cycling and walking; summer shifts the emphasis toward the coast and later evenings. Three or four days is enough for a weekend, while a week permits slower beach time. The budget is mid-range, with good scope to mix casual market meals and paid attractions. Explore the old town, cross the Turia gardens by foot or bicycle, visit the City of Arts and Sciences, spend an afternoon at the beach and plan one long rice-based lunch.",
      "image": "assets/destinations/valencia-hero.webp",
